    intro: "This week the class sits the final examination. We have studied that Christ is the resurrection and the life, that death is defeated, that believers are with Christ at death and will be raised, that God will judge the world in righteousness, that believers are justified by faith, that final punishment is a solemn reality on which Christians hold differing views, that heaven and the new creation are our hope, and how to grieve, prepare for death, respond to popular beliefs and live with eternity in view.",
    context: "The final examination is built from the approved question bank for this course following the curriculum blueprint. It includes multiple choice, true or false and short answer questions. Scores help determine eligibility for the course certificate according to your church's pass mark. The most important preparation is prayerful reflection on how you are living what you have learned.",
